  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 139 AM EDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nPatchy early morning fog will be possible again today, but it should \nbe mainly near rivers and lakes. \n\nWe remain in a persistent pattern of a large upper ridge centered to \nour west and surface high pressure extending into our area from the \nnorth and northeast.  This will continue to provide dry weather \nthrough the weekend and well into next week.  Models generally show \nat least some suppression of the upper ridge in the mid week time \nframe with short wave energy moving through the Great Lakes region, \nbut precipitation currently looks likely to remain well to our north \nwith dry weather continuing for our area through next Thursday.  \n\nFor the entire period we can expect cool nights and pleasant \nafternoons with high temperatures each day not far off of seasonal \nnormals. We will also see low relative humidity values during the \nafternoon hours, but light winds will help to mitigate fire weather \nconcerns.",
